Sun Nov 15 20:07:04 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- build the release binary without the test harness: openSUSE %meson
  passes --auto-features=enabled, which turns the harness option's
  "auto" into "enabled", so -DUMBRIEL_HARNESS was defined and 12
  test-only IPC commands (clock-freeze, renderer-recover, plane-cursor,
  ...) shipped in the release package. Upstream compiles them out of
  anything but a debug build
- require xwayland instead of xwayland-satellite: upstream PACKAGING.md
  needs the Xwayland binary on PATH for wlroots' Xwayland (zero
  references to xwayland-satellite anywhere in the tree); added to the
  Debian recipe's Depends as well

